claim.claim-text:
a fixed contact (52) and a movable contact (54);
a magnetic actuator (58) coupled to the movable contact (54), the magnetic actuator (58) configured, under a first energization, to move the moveable contact (54) against the bias of at least one spring (66, 78) coupled to the movable contact (54) towards the fixed contact (52), wherein AC current conducts across a gap (56) formed between the movable contact (54) and the fixed contact (52) as the moveable contact (54) is moved toward the fixed contact (52) and before the movable contact (54) and the fixed contact (52) make contact; and
the magnetic actuator (58), under a second energization, being further configured when the movable contact (54) makes contact with the fixed contact (52) to allow the bias of the at least one spring (66, 78) to move the movable contact (54) away from the fixed contact (52) so that the amount of time that the current conducts between the movable contact (54) and the fixed contact (52) is about one fundamental frequency cycle, and preferably, about one-half of one fundamental frequency cycle of the current, wherein second energization of the magnetic actuator (58) occurs at a time so that when the movable contact (54) and the fixed contact (52) begin conducting an applied voltage on the switch assembly (50) is at or near a peak of the voltage wave so that the current is symmetric.
